In <103147@convex.convex.com>, swarren@convex.com (Steve Warren) writes:
>So as long as you are using the lower-case movement commands you will
>never attack or jump into water (unless blind or confused or hallucinating).
><shft>-move is an aggressive move and *will* move you into water and will
>attack any neighboring creature.  <ctl>-move would act the same as it
>currently does.  <ctl>-<shft>-move would combine the extended movement
>mode of <ctl> with the aggressive mode of <shft>, reproducing the same
>mode of movement as the current <shft>-move (for anyone crazy enough to
>want to move this way)  ;^).

I like this sort of idea - <ctrl><shift> doesn't work on all terminals, though.
How about lifting something from PC HACK 1.0.3, where the Scroll Lock key turns
"fast play" mode on and off - sort of like playing with the SHIFT key held down
in current versions. We could probably use the "_" character - I don't think
this one is used at the moment.

I'd also like to see confirmation of the "!" command - my .cshrc takes a wee
while to run, and if I hit ! by mistake, I have to wait until it's finished
running before I can carry on playing...

